## 2. What changed

No file under `src/`, no file under `docs/`, the recolour formula and the bake stay as they are.
The change is in three asset sources only.

### Ball (commit de94485e)

`assets/ball.ts`, the lit leather:

```
-    let c = rgb(k.tint(slot, 0.03 + 0.05 * sheen)); // the lit leather
+    let c = rgb(k.tint(slot, -0.06 * (1 - sheen)));
```

The leather keeps the slot colour and darkens by 6 % where the sheen is low. A positive shade
mixes toward white in linear light, so the stored texel was not the slot colour, and the recolour
rule multiplied that gap by the option ratio. A negative shade is a multiply, and the recolour
rule keeps it. The seam #5a4030 and the floor shadow #6f503a keep their fixed colours. The
shape, the four gores, the dent and the five presets do not change.

Result: `node scripts/preset-colour-check.mjs ball` exits 0. Every slot lands on its option. The
anchor error is 5 to 7 of 255 and the formula residual is 0 or 1. The mean default texel is now
#d64339 against the slot default #d9443a, and the redyellow preset mean moved from #db5e58 (a
drift of 29.6) to #d64339 (a drift of 2.7). The ball measures 0.16 x 0.16 x 0.159 m and holds
1,184 triangles, the same as before.

### Kite (commit 86debd54)

`assets/kite.ts`, the sail paint. Two deviations from the first brief. Both are recorded here
and in `briefs/kite.md`.

1. The lower-sail shadow is gone, on the PM decision of 2026-11-18. The lit upper sail was
   already changed from `k.tint(slot, 0.10)` to `k.tint(slot, 0)`. The sail is now the pure slot
   colour everywhere, and the render light gives the shading.
2. The cream edge binding and the cream tape cross have a crisp edge. The soft edge is gone.

Deviation 2 came from the first kite build of this round. After the shadow was removed, the
check still named kite/yellow/sailA with an anchor error of 15 of 255, and the mean error was
only 0.16. A probe over the baked atlas (the stored default texel, the stored preset texel and
the mask byte of every eligible texel) showed the cause. 149,366 anchor texels hold the exact
default 217,68,58. About 600 anchor texels hold a colour up to 6 of 255 away from it, and the
worst ones hold 217,74,64 with the mask byte 253. The stored green is 6 above the default
because the soft cream edge had mixed about 1.4 % of cream into that texel, and the cream
#efe6d2 is far from the slot colour in green. The recolour rule multiplies that gap by the
option ratio, and the red to yellow ratio in green is 9.33, so a texel 6 of 255 from the
default landed 15 of 255 from the option.

A soft edge always leaves texels in that band, because the cream fraction rises from 0 to 1
along the edge. The engine ties the colour mix to the tint mask, so no blend can move the cream
out of the band while the texel stays eligible. The crisp edge keeps every slot texel at the
exact slot colour: the cream texels have a mask of 0 and the slot texels a mask of 1. The band
widths are the same as before: the binding covers the rim within 19 mm of the outline, the
spine tape within 15 mm of the spine and the spreader tape within 13 mm of the spreader.

Result: `node scripts/preset-colour-check.mjs kite` exits 0. Every slot of every preset lands
on its option with an anchor error of 0, a mean error of 0 and a formula residual of 0. The
yellow preset no longer has a lemon quarter and the red preset no longer has a rose quarter.
The kite measures 0.359 x 0.930 x 0.041 m and holds 5,150 triangles, the same as before.

### Brush (commit 2cff4c97)

`assets/brush.ts`, the acceptance finding N3 of the group 2 rework. The paint tip was 76 px at
1024 px/m and the brush read as a fat pencil.

- The paint covers the bristles from the tip up to the ferrule edge. Every bristle surface below
  the ferrule is the `paint` slot colour, and no cream is left. The cream constants
  `BRISTLE` and `BRISTLE_SHADE` are gone.
- The bristle radius grows by 20 %: the cone goes from 3.2 mm to 3.84 mm at the tip and from
  12.8 mm to 15.36 mm at the ferrule edge, and the round tip grows from 3.2 mm to 3.84 mm.
- The length of 0.17 m, the handle, the grip band, the iron ferrule, the lean of 8 degrees and
  the two presets (pink #e87fb0, purple #8e5bb5) stay.

Result: the pink tip reads at 128 px on the sprite sheet. The brush measures 0.046 x 0.169 x
0.031 m and holds 1,588 triangles. mech-check: exit 0, ok true, bottomY -0.001, no warning line.

